Step-by-Step Execution Flow

When you run this app, here's exactly what happens:

Step 1: App Component Loads

• The App component is the first to load • React renders it and executes all the code inside

Step 2: State is Initialized

• The
useState
hook creates the
users
state with three user objects • This data is now stored in memory and ready to be used

Step 3: JSX is Evaluated

• React evaluates the JSX return statement • It sees the header section (static content) • It sees the cards-grid div • It sees the map() function that loops through users

Step 4: map() Loops Through Users

• For each user in the array, React creates a
<UserProfileCard />
component: • First iteration: Creates card for Alice (id: 1) • Second iteration: Creates card for Bob (id: 2) • Third iteration: Creates card for Carol (id: 3)

Step 5: Props are Passed

• For each card, React passes: •
key={user.id}
- React's internal identifier •
user={user}
- The user object data

Step 6: UserProfileCard Component Renders

• Each UserProfileCard component receives the user prop and renders: • Avatar image from user.avatar • Name from user.name • Role from user.role • Bio from user.bio • Email and join date from user details • Two action buttons

Step 7: CSS Styling is Applied

• The CSS file styles all the components: • Cards get white background and shadow • Grid layout arranges them responsively • Hover effects make them interactive • Buttons get styled with colors and transitions

Step 8: Browser Displays the App

• The user sees: • Purple gradient background • Header with title • Three beautiful user cards in a grid • Cards lift up when hovered • Buttons are interactive and styled

